", ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/RetryByCountStrategy","text":"RetryByCountStrategy","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent20RetryByCountStrategyC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Equatable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SQ","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The maximum number of times to retry the upstream, defaulting to 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"retries"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The specific error that should trigger a retry.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"error"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that emits the same output as the upstream but retries on the specified error up to the specified number of times."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method returns an "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that retries the upstream only when the specified error occurs, up to the given number of retries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not all "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":"s can be retried. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be retried on their own."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["actor CallCounter {","    private(set) var count = 0","    func increment() -> Int {","        count += 1","        return count","    }","}","","enum CustomError: Error, Equatable {","    case temporaryFailure","}","","let counter = CallCounter()","","let sequence = DeferredTask {","    let attempt = await counter.increment()","    if attempt < 2 {","        throw CustomError.temporaryFailure","    } else if attempt == 2 {","        throw NSError(domain: \"OtherError\", code: 1, userInfo: nil)","    }","    return 7","}",".toAsyncSequence()",".retry(3, on: CustomError.temporaryFailure)","","for try await value in sequence {","    print(value) \/\/ prints 7 after retry","}"]},{"type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" can be retried, for this to work the sequence has to implement an iterator that doesn’t preserve state across various creations."}]}],"style":"important"},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncThrowingStream"},{"type":"text","text":" are notable sequences which cannot be retried on their own."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}]}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"url":"\/documentation\/afluent","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","kind":"symbol","title":"Afluent"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/RetryOn":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RetryOn","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AsyncSequences.RetryOn","identifie